sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Uriz et al. (2003) & Aizenberg et al. (2005) sponge spicule silicatein axial symmetry, concentric biosilica lamination, and Euplectella checkerboard lattice mechanics — MorphoEval overall 48.7/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py` (consensus score 52.6/100). The v1 script computes static unit ray vectors for O_h hexactins (90 deg) and T_d tetractins (109.47 deg) along with a 1D lamellar thinning curve, but lacks a 3D diffusion-reaction biosilica accretion solver across monaxon, triactine, tetractin, and hexactin filaments, omits silicatein-inhibited ablation controls, omits *Euplectella* alternating checkerboard diagonal lattice shear stiffness analysis, omits 12-species cross-taxa Porifera validation, and does not load or segment the vendored *Euplectella aspergillum* specimen image. Overall 48.7/100 (faithfulness 41.3, reproducibility 65.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 24, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 50, Source and data traceability 64, Code-to-model traceability 62, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: docs/media/sponge_spicule_hexactin_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-bavestrello-sponge-spicule-hexactin.py at HEAD, image/png, 137945 B, 1278×584 px, artifact_sha256 483d6b704516bf84cc1c8b19e78bac055ce86a7f3b9ca3c9f8e46db339204f21 (sha256 483d6b704516bf84cc1c8b19e78bac055ce86a7f3b9ca3c9f8e46db339204f21), spec_fingerprint a5bee59a94597f4d966c69c524721cb2d57ff58a497dff220c73adc1f47687dd. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a5bee59a94597f4d966c69c524721cb2d57ff58a497dff220c73adc1f47687dd; artifact_sha256: 483d6b704516bf84cc1c8b19e78bac055ce86a7f3b9ca3c9f8e46db339204f21; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/euplectella_aspergillum_specimen.jpg=b56275f43e5ea078..., datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/scout_manifest.json=fb6e06653d9d14ac..., datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/sponge_spicule_hexactin_reference.json=b9dd33b60b05730c...}." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expose full CLI parameter overrides (`--d-s`, `--k-cat`, `--r-core`, `--n-lamellae`, `--seed`, `--skip-gif`), upgrade `self_test()` to an 8-point verification suite with bitwise two-run determinism, and render a 6-panel publication-grade synthesis figure and co-evolving 2-panel 3D spicule & lamellar growth GIF.",
            "remediation needed: Implement a 3D silicatein-catalyzed diffusion-reaction biosilica accretion solver (`simulate_spicule_biosilica_accretion_3d`) across all 5 Porifera spicule symmetry & ablation regimes: (1) silicatein-inhibited ablation negative control (k_cat = 0 -> 0 accreted rays), (2) Demospongiae monaxon/oxea (D_inf_h, 2 rays, 180 deg), (3) Calcarea planar triactine (D_3h, 3 rays, 120 deg), (4) Demospongiae tetrahedral tetractin/calthrop (T_d, 4 rays, arccos(-1/3) = 109.4712 deg), and (5) Hexactinellida cubic hexactin (O_h, 6 orthogonal rays, 90 deg).",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/sponge_spicule_hexactin/` at runtime and perform computer-vision Difference-of-Gaussians strut orientation and lattice-pitch segmentation (`segment_euplectella_specimen`) on `euplectella_aspergillum_specimen.jpg`, measuring orthogonal hexactin intersection angle (89.65 deg vs 90 deg), diagonal bracing angle (47.68 deg vs 45 deg), and square grid pitch (24.07 px = 2.50 mm).",
            "remediation needed: Model concentric silica cylinder lamination (h_n = h_1 * r_1 / r_n, fracture toughness amplification G_lam / G_mono = 1 + eta_deflect * N_layers) and *Euplectella* alternating open/closed checkerboard diagonal lattice shear stiffness K_shear(f_diag) vs unbraced square grids, and validate inter-ray angles and lamellar toughness scaling across all 12 empirical Porifera species in `sponge_spicule_hexactin_reference.json`." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.487"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Pass 1 baseline assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

